# The program makes a Parcel in two ways: { weight, fragile } and { weight, insured }. The arms of the walk over own keys ask for the orders at which the makers stop.
# They asked for the whole declared order and for the required fields alone: { weight, fragile, insured } and { weight }: both tests failed in every turn.
# Nothing but `length` reads the list, so the read stands in the arms: behind the tests it is a constant, and the list is made on the closed arm alone.
# What is read out of the list of parcels may be undefined, so the layout is not proven: the test of the shape stands in front.
# RUN: walk f2 mechanisms=all
# CHECK-LABEL: code f2:Body
# CHECK: isLoopHead=true
# CHECK: ShapeTest
# CHECK: HasKeyOrder {{*}}fields=[2, 0]
# CHECK: HasKeyOrder {{*}}fields=[2, 1]
# RUN(LISTS): walk f2 mechanisms=all
# LISTS-LABEL: code f2:Body
# LISTS-NOT: = NewArray [[weight]], [[other]] contents="
# RUN(ANSWERS): run-in-shell mechanisms=all
# ANSWERS: 10
